Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:47:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] sr-aef: drop a lookup that only aalt used, now that aalt
 has its rules

With its rules written into aalt, a lookup nothing else references was still
written out on its own, so the compiled font carried it twice (aalt's copy
and an unused one) and every later lookup moved down the list.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
---
 sr-aef/resources/aalt.fea |   4 ++++
 sr-aef/resources/aalt.ttf | Bin 540 -> 556 bytes
 sr-aef/src/lib.rs         |  36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sr-aef/resources/aalt.fea b/sr-aef/resources/aalt.fea
index 5cd1a10f..381a7ad0 100644
--- a/sr-aef/resources/aalt.fea
+++ b/sr-aef/resources/aalt.fea
@@ -12,3 +12,7 @@ feature aalt {
     lookup single;
     lookup alternate;
 } aalt;
+
+feature salt {
+    lookup single;
+} salt;
